NOTICE — third-party assets and trained weights

The MIT grant above covers the SOURCE CODE in this repository. It does not, and
cannot, relicense the datasets or pretrained models this project depends on.

1. TRAINED WEIGHTS ARE NON-COMMERCIAL.

   `data/models/general.npz` is fitted partly on the `calib_ood` carve of
   So-Fake-OOD, which is CC BY-NC 4.0. The weights are therefore a derivative of
   NonCommercial data and must be treated as NON-COMMERCIAL, research and
   evaluation use only, regardless of the MIT grant on the code.

   `tampered.npz`, `face.npz`, `spectral.npz` and `text_crop.npz` are fitted on
   SID_Set only (CC BY 4.0) and carry an attribution requirement rather than a
   non-commercial one.

2. NO DATASET IMAGES ARE REDISTRIBUTED HERE.

   This repository contains no corpus imagery. The embedding cache lives in a
   private Hugging Face repository and is shared with team members only.
   `.dockerignore` is an allowlist that keeps `data/` out of the public demo
   image; it is a licence boundary, not a size optimisation.

3. DATASETS USED, AND THEIR TERMS.

   SID_Set              CC BY 4.0        huggingface.co/datasets/saberzl/SID_Set
   So-Fake-OOD          CC BY-NC 4.0     huggingface.co/datasets/saberzl/So-Fake-OOD
   WildFake             no licence stated on the ModelScope mirror used;
                        treated as research use only
   COCO 2017            images under their original Flickr terms;
                        annotations CC BY 4.0 — cocodataset.org/#termsofuse
   LAION-5B             CC BY 4.0 metadata; images are linked, not owned

4. PRETRAINED MODELS USED, AND THEIR TERMS.

   CLIP ViT-L/14        MIT — github.com/openai/CLIP
   open_clip            MIT — github.com/mlfoundations/open_clip
   YuNet                MIT — opencv/opencv_zoo, models/face_detection_yunet
                        (Wu, Peng & Yu 2023; orig. ShiqiYu/libfacedetection.train)
   RapidOCR / PP-OCRv4  Apache 2.0

5. BASELINES ARE NOT VENDORED.

   CNNDetection (Wang et al., CVPR 2020) and FatFormer (Liu et al., CVPR 2024)
   are downloaded at their released weights for comparison in
   `scripts/compare_baselines.py`. Neither is redistributed here, and each
   remains under its own licence.

No TikTok trademark, logo or branding is used anywhere in this repository or in
the demo.
